  "notes": [
    "Irregular reflexive -IR verb with an *e→i* stem change throughout the present (except nosotros) and in the 3rd person Pretérito Indefinido — same pattern as *reñir*",
    "The *i* is dropped after *ñ* in the 3rd person preterite: *se tiñó* (not ~~se tiñió~~), *se tiñeron* (not ~~se tiñieron~~) — the ñ already contains the \"y\" glide, so a separate written *i* would be redundant",
    "-IR e→i verbs keep the stem change in subjuntivo nosotros: *nos tiñamos*",
    "Affirmative imperative attaches the reflexive pronoun with a written accent to preserve stress: *tíñete, tíñase, tiñámonos, tíñanse*; negative imperative keeps the pronoun separate: *no te tiñas*...",
    "Past participle: *teñido* (regular)",
    "Means \"to dye one's hair\" or \"to get (something) dyed\" — *se tiñó el pelo de rojo* (she dyed her hair red)",
    "Base verb *teñir* (non-reflexive, \"to dye\" something else) follows the identical stem-change pattern: *teñir una camisa* (to dye a shirt)",
    "Related: *tinte* (dye, tint), *teñido/a* (dyed), *tintorería* (dry cleaner's, dyer's shop)"
  ],
